# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# API credentials, local TLS material, and linked browser sessions.
config/api_keys.json
config/certs/
config/whatsapp_web/
.kira_whatsapp_profile/
.jarvis_profiles/
# OAuth tokens and client secrets.
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
memory/kira_tasks.json
memory/kira_startup_state.json
config/dashboard_devices.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# Historical patch backups and one-time patch utilities.
/backup_kira_*/
*.pre_*
/apply_kira_*.py
/configure_kira_groq_free_sslfix.py
/Desktop/

config/providers.json
config/autochat.json
memory/api_usage.json
